* 2015: Excellence in Teaching Award, The Ohio State University College of Public Health<ref>{{cite web |last= Filby |first= Max |date= June 14, 2020 |title= As Ohio health director, Dr. Amy Acton went from unknown to icon during coronavirus pandemic |url= https://www.newarkadvocate.com/story/news/local/2020/06/14/ohio-health-director-dr-amy-acton-went-unknown-icon/3177932001/ |work= The Columbus Dispatch |language= en-US |access-date= March 22, 2023}}</ref>
* 2021: Profile in Courage Award, [[John F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum]]<ref>{{cite web |title= Celebrating COVID Courage |url= https://www.jfklibrary.org/events-and-awards/profile-in-courage-award/award-recipients/covid-courage |publisher= John F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum |access-date= June 28, 2022}}</ref>
* 2022: Ohio Honoree, ''[[USA Today]]''{{'}}s Women of the Year<ref>{{cite web |title= Meet USA TODAY's Women of the Year |url= https://www.usatoday.com/storytelling/grid/women-of-the-year-2022/ |website= USA Today |language= en-US |date= March 28, 2022 |access-date= June 28, 2022}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
In 1989, Amy married Douglas Beech, with whom she had three children.<ref name= "stirland" /><ref>{{cite web |title= GERALD STEARNS Obituary (1938 - 2015) - Las Vegas, NV - Las Vegas Review-Journal |url= https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/lvrj/name/gerald-stearns-obituary?id=18425259 |website= Legacy.com |access-date= April 21, 2026}}</ref> The couple divorced in 2008.<ref>{{cite web |last= Rowland |first= Darrel |title= Fact check: Ex-Ohio health director Amy Acton has no ties to abortion charities, clinic |url= https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/06/23/fact-check-ohios-amy-acton-has-no-ties-abortion-charities-clinic/3241600001/ |website= USA Today |language= en-US |access-date= November 16, 2025}}</ref>

In 2010, she married Eric Acton, a middle-school teacher and track coach, who had three children from a previous marriage.<ref name="ThePulse-2019" /><ref>{{cite web |date= March 28, 2026 |title= Exclusive {{!}} Put me in, coach! Ohio Dem candidate's sprint to marry her son's cross country coach five months after his divorce |url= https://nypost.com/2026/03/28/us-news/put-me-in-coach-ohio-dem-candidates-sprint-to-marry-her-sons-cross-country-coach-five-months-after-his-divorce/ |language= en-US |access-date= May 4, 2026}}</ref> Together, they have a blended family of six children.<ref name="Miller-2020" /><ref name="Bischoff-2019" />

Acton resides with her family in [[Bexley, Ohio]].<ref name="Gordon-2020" /><ref name="Bischoff-2019" /> She is [[Jewish]], and her husband and his children are [[Episcopal Church (United States)|Episcopalian]].<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.clevelandjewishnews.com/news/local_news/dr-amy-acton-says-virtual-seder-was-healing-in-a-time-of-covid-19/article_22809840-7b27-11ea-b723-37e35802ff18.html |title= Dr. Amy Acton says virtual seder was 'healing' in a time of COVID-19 |last= Kaufman |first= Jane |date= April 10, 2020 |website= Cleveland Jewish News |access-date= April 21, 2020}}</ref>

